	(text "1 inputs: SDET_P, threshold network SDET_N"
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 101.6 78 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "71150cc3-b50a-496a-b130-3e4282eff13c")
	)
	(text "Design intent (revision 2, decision 12; nothing here is simulated or measured)\nPROPOSED   The signal arrives already AC coupled and referenced to VCM_REF (Front End sheet). With 8b/10b the\n           eye centre is that baseline, so IN- is the same baseline plus a small trim: no peak tracking. Light\n           on makes SDET_P go BELOW the baseline (OPA857 output swings down, SBOS630D p.19), so LVDS_P is LOW\n           for a one: the FPGA must invert, or LVDS_P/N be swapped at the FPGA.\nPROPOSED   Threshold SDET_N: R84 1k from VCM_REF (matches the 1k return R59 on IN+, so bias currents cancel:\n           IB -1 uA typ / +-5 uA max, IOS +-1 uA, SNOSDA2F p.7; a single 1k would give 1 mV typ / 5 mV max,\n           10k would give 10 / 50 mV). DAC_TH through R85 100k: trim = (DAC - VCM_REF) x 1k/101k, so a 0 to\n           3.3 V DAC with VCM_REF 1.65 V moves the threshold +-16.3 mV (8 uV per 12-bit LSB). C84 10n to GND\n           keeps IN- quiet (corner 16 kHz). VTH_MON = SDET_N through R86 10k for the ADC.\nPROPOSED   External hysteresis (research 2-4 mV; the internal LE/HYS pin cannot go below about 8 mV, SNOSDA2F\n           p.8, Fig. 7-4 p.16): positive feedback from OUT+ to IN+ through R87 5.49k in series with C87 100p.\n           OUT+ swings 350 mVpp (VOD 350 mV typ, VOCM 1.2 V, p.7). Source seen at IN+ at signal speed = 49.9\n           ohm (R56) || 1k (R59) = 47.5 ohm. Window = 350 mV x 47.5/(5490 + 47.5) = 3.0 mV. C87 blocks DC: a\n           bare resistor would shift IN+ by (1.2 - 1.65) x 1k/(1k + 5.49k) = -69 mV. High-pass corner 1/(2 pi\n           x 5.54k x 100p) = 287 kHz, tau 554 ns, so a 100 ns run (5 UI) keeps 83 % of the window. The spec\n           text of about 100k with a 1k source only holds for slow (DC) states: at 50 MHz edges it gives 0.17\n           mV. UNRESOLVED: effect on jitter not simulated.\nPROPOSED   LE/HYS (pin 8) left open = internal hysteresis 0 mV and latch off (p.8). R82 150k to GND (30 mV,\n           DNP) and R83 0R to LE_HYS (DNP) are footprints only. SHDN (pin 7): R81 10k pull-up, SHDN_N active\n           low (VIH 1.5 V, VIL 0.4 V, p.8); shutdown is not a guaranteed zero output (standing correction 11).\nVERIFIED   VCCI = VCCO = 3V3 (2.4 to 5.5 V, p.19); 100 nF 0402 + 1 uF at each of VCCI and VCCO, VCCO through\n           R80 0R (bead option). VEE and EP to GND (datasheet gives no pad requirement beyond a ground plane).\n           PWR_FLAG on the VCCO net because R80 is passive.\nPROPOSED   LVDS: OUT+ = LVDS_P, OUT- = LVDS_N; 100 ohm termination R180 across the A/B inputs of the fan-out\n           buffer U50 on the Connector sheet, a few cm away (revision 4; SN65LVDS104 has no on-chip\n           termination, LVDS104 p.16 Fig. 25; the ECP5 end is terminated with DIFFRESISTOR,\n           docs/research/ulx3s-lvds-input.md). TP20 SDET_N, TP21 SDET_P (DNP, the probe loads the input).\nUNRESOLVED Comparator input noise and delay below 10 mV overdrive are not in the datasheet\n           (docs/research/post-amp-slicer.md section 1); IB at VCM = 1.65 V is not specified."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 101.6 172 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "76cbd136-832b-4a1b-8152-b6e727c6829f")
	)
